From 917fee7be9860d940b8d18e3f81672803ee496f1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tiesa Meskis <tiesa@meskis.net>
Date: Mon, 24 Aug 2026 18:09:49 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(muk_web_theme): disable AppsMenu override for Odoo 19
 compatibility

Odoo 19 rewrote the Dropdown component (dropdown.js) to be fully
popover-based with no XML template. The content slot is now passed
as props to a DropdownPopover component mounted via usePopover,
rather than rendered conditionally inline via t-if.

AppsMenu extends Dropdown, so it inherits this new architecture.
The old approach of replacing <Dropdown> in web.NavBar.AppsMenu
via xpath no longer works:
  - //Dropdown xpath fails because Owl's template engine lowercases
    component element names when parsing as HTML DOM
  - The content slot renders into the DOM immediately on page load
    rather than only when the dropdown is open, because the popover
    lifecycle differs from the old t-if approach
    Bootstrap's display:none on .dropdown-menu

For Odoo 19: disable the AppsMenu template override and component
registration. The systray ResizeObserver fix in navbar.js is kept
as it remains valid.

TODO: rewrite AppsMenu as a standalone component using usePopover
directly (not extending Dropdown) to restore the full-screen app
launcher overlay on Odoo 19.
